   $q$Which revision of sentence 11 would best conclude the draft?$q$, $q$[{"text":"In conclusion, Mbeki describes a league where players touched the ball three times as often.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"evidence-without-analysis"},{"text":"In conclusion, small fields cost towns less money to build and to keep mowed.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Mbeki's evidence shows that small fields give young players more touches and faster choices, which helps them grow.","is_correct":true},{"text":"In conclusion, soccer is fun, and every kid should try playing it at least once.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opinion-not-analysis"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Mbeki's evidence shows that small fields give young players more touches and faster choices, which helps them grow.$q$, $q$The best conclusion pulls together both reasons from the draft, more touches and faster choices. Repeating the league's numbers only restates one piece of evidence and does not wrap up the analysis.$q$, 'draft', '9ddeec85-6a0e-54b0-b4a3-cb4c9f2dc948')
