-- Passage wg6-writing-with-evidence-p05
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('1f43b476-1777-55fc-a3eb-dd2219c2ef77', 'wg6-writing-with-evidence-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g6-writing-with-evidence'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Draft: Students Plan the Lunch Menu$q$, $q$(1) In "What's for Lunch? Ask the Students," Rosa Delgado describes a middle school that let students help plan the cafeteria menu. (2) ____. (3) Delgado reports that before the change, the school threw away about forty pounds of food every day. (4) After students tasted new recipes and voted on them, the amount dropped to about fifteen pounds. (5) This drop shows that students ate more of the food once they had helped choose it.

(6) Delgado also shows that the plan taught students new skills. (7) Student planners had to keep each meal within a set budget and include a fruit or vegetable. (8) One student told Delgado that planning a week of lunches was "harder than any math worksheet." (9) Pizza is served on Fridays at my school. (10) These details show that the students learned to balance cost, health, and taste.

(11) ____.$q$, 'draft')
