   $q$Which sentence best fills blank (2) as the claim of the draft?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Haddad says that the walk to school in the town took about twenty minutes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Haddad shows that a walking school bus got more children walking and helped them start the day ready to learn.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Haddad believes that all school buses should be replaced with walking groups.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Some children walk to school each morning, and other children ride in cars.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-claim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Haddad shows that a walking school bus got more children walking and helped them start the day ready to learn.$q$, $q$Paragraph 1 shows more children walking and paragraph 2 shows students arriving ready to learn, so the claim needs both ideas. The draft never says Haddad wants to replace all buses, so that choice is not supported.$q$, 'draft', '4145b0d4-eca2-5924-b2ff-879bc4c161c0')
