   $q$Which sentence best fills blank (2) as the claim of the draft?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Brennan believes that cameras should not be allowed in any science class.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Brennan describes a scientist who drew the same leaf for one whole week.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Brennan shows that drawing helps scientists notice more details and remember them for longer.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Scientists study many different things, such as leaves, insects, and rocks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-claim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Brennan shows that drawing helps scientists notice more details and remember them for longer.$q$, $q$Paragraph 1 is about noticing details and paragraph 2 is about remembering them, so the claim should name both. The leaf example is only one piece of evidence, so it is too narrow to be the claim.$q$, 'draft', '1df309dc-4cad-5393-b532-525f091910cf')
